==Effects and upgrades==
:''For a list of monsters affected by the salve amulet, [[Undead (attribute)|see here]].''
The salve amulet's bonuses against the undead '''do not''' stack with the [[black mask]] and [[Slayer helmet|slayer helmet's]] 16.67% attack and strength bonuses; wearing both will only apply the bonuses of the salve amulet. However, the bonuses of [[Void Knight equipment]] '''do''' stack. Additionally, the amulet's effects apply to all targets when using multi-hitting melee weapons in a [[multicombat area]], such as the [[Scythe of Vitur]] and the [[special attack]] of the [[dragon 2h sword]].

The salve amulet can also be upgraded through enchanting and imbuing it:
* Enchanting the amulet increases the amulet's undead bonus from 16.67% to 20%. This requires using [[Tarn's diary]], acquired as part of the [[Lair of Tarn Razorlor]] miniquest.
* Imbuing the amulet extends the undead bonus to ranged (16.67%) and magic attacks (15%). This requires using either 800,000 [[Nightmare Zone]] [[Nightmare Zone#Rewards|points]] (halved upon completing the [[Combat Achievements/Hard|hard combat achievements]]), 320 [[Soul Wars]] [[Zeal Tokens]], or by using a [[scroll of imbuing]] on the amulet.
** Amulets imbued through the latter two methods do '''not''' count for completing the [[Ardougne Diary]] task.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1355871771208134657|date=31 January 2021|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/107617|archivedate=5 February 2021|quote=No, the Soul Wars version is a different item from the NMZ item, and it doesn't do a task check.}} Furthermore, amulets imbued at one location cannot be refunded at a different location.

